 a likely peak near 32–33 °C, driven by persistent subtropical high pressure, clear to partly cloudy skies, and strong urban heat-island amplification in the Kanto plain. Recent model runs from the Japan Meteorological Agency and global ensembles indicate modest day-to-day variability tied to timing of any scattered showers or changes in boundary-layer mixing; lighter winds and higher dew points favor the upper end of the 31–34 °C range while increased cloud cover or sea-breeze effects could cap readings near 31 °C. Historical late-July climatology places average daily maxima around 31–32 °C, providing a baseline against which current model consensus is being weighed by traders.","context_requires_regen":true,"context_updated_at":"2026-07-22T05:00:10.803Z"}}],"ready":false,"funded":false,"acceptingOrdersTimestamp":"2026-07-22T04:03:00Z","cyom":false,"competitive":0.8003199679231757,"pagerDutyNotificationEnabled":false,"approved":true,"rewardsMinSize":50,"rewardsMaxSpread":4.5,"spread":0.001,"lastTradePrice":0.001,"bestAsk":0.001,"automaticallyActive":true,"clearBookOnStart":false,"manualActivation":false,"negRiskOther":false,"umaResolutionStatuses":"[]","pendingDeployment":false,"deploying":false,"deployingTimestamp":"2026-07-22T04:02:45.028502Z","rfqEnabled":false,"holdingRewardsEnabled":false,"feesEnabled":true,"requiresTranslation":false,"feeType":"weather_fees","feeSchedule":{"exponent":1,"rate":0.05,"takerOnly":true,"rebateRate":0.25}}
